@Navid200 The slope is correct, yes. Also that there are only a few different arrows (flat, 45 degrees, up, double up) is not the point.

xDrip uploads the BG values with a device name, the delta, the arrow and other informations, e.g.:
```
{"_id":"602d79d301181286acc396af","device":"xDrip-DexcomG5 G5 Native","date":1613593041389,"dateString":"2021-02-17T20:17:21.389Z","sgv":226,"delta":8,"direction":"FortyFiveUp","type":"sgv","filtered":0,"unfiltered":0,"rssi":100,"noise":1,"sysTime":"2021-02-17T20:17:21.389Z","utcOffset":60,"mills":1613593041389}
```
Also sometimes the uploaded delta isn't correct and doesn't represent the real delta to the previous uploaded value.
